    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup is anchored by **Lawrence Butler**, who commands the highest score of the day at 72.82. Facing Kumar Rocker, **Butler** benefits from a strong park factor and a favorable platoon advantage, making him our primary engine for power and run production. **Jonathan Aranda** follows closely with a 70.47, as he is perfectly positioned against the vulnerable 4.91 xERA of Bassitt. While **Zack Gelof** is also drawing a plus matchup against Rocker, his scoring is tempered slightly by the right-on-right dynamic, though he remains a strong start in the three-hole. We are tracking several \"Lineup Pending\" statuses, including **Cal Raleigh** and **Brendan Donovan**; if either drops significantly in the order, their efficiency scores will likely slide toward our 40-point threshold.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was excluding **Braden Montgomery**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 39.41 rating. While he possesses an appealing park factor, the matchup against the 3.28 xERA of Jobe presents too much risk for a player who hasn't quite cleared our mandatory 40-point \"Zebras Floor.\" Similarly, **Gavin Sheets** sits at 39.12; despite a positive platoon bump, he is grounded by a tough matchup against Williams. **Jung Hoo Lee** remains in the active lineup despite a mediocre 51.14 score, largely because the wind blowing out adds enough potential upside to his leadoff duties to keep him above the benching threshold. With **Will Smith** currently sidelined on the IL, our roster depth is being tested, but these calculated projections ensure we maximize our daily caps while avoiding the downside of starters facing elite pitching like the 3.91 xERA of George Kirby, which keeps **Daulton Varsho** in a more modest scoring tier.",
